WEBVTT

00:18:26.847 --> 00:18:30.555
it sounds like it's also transformational
for the community that they are in.

00:18:30.579 --> 00:18:33.949
Fundamentally, what they're doing
is building connections,

00:18:33.973 --> 00:18:37.268
creating possibilities for other people,
listening to other people,

00:18:37.292 --> 00:18:40.377
helping other people
find their own weaving capability.

00:18:40.401 --> 00:18:42.243
DB: I've really come to the conclusion

00:18:42.267 --> 00:18:44.326
that the neighborhood
is the unit of change,

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.500
not the individual.

00:18:45.524 --> 00:18:47.818
A friend of mine from
Shreveport, Louisiana says,

00:18:47.842 --> 00:18:51.258
"You can't only clean the part
of the swimming pool you're swimming in.

00:18:51.282 --> 00:18:53.052
You've got to clean the whole pool."

00:18:53.076 --> 00:18:55.665
CA: So, this really strikes me
as an interesting idea,

00:18:55.689 --> 00:18:57.947
and perhaps is the key
to the later connection

00:18:57.971 --> 00:19:00.283
to some of your political thinking.